  "solution": {
    "approach": "Use nested loops to iterate through rows and columns, printing characters corresponding to the pattern formula.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(N^2)",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(N^2)",
    "code": {
      "C": "#include <stdio.h>\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    if (scanf(\"%d\", &n) == 1) {\n        for (int i = n; i >= 1; i--) {\n            for (int j = 1; j <= i; j++) printf(\"%d\", j);\n            printf(\"\\n\");\n        }\n    }\n    return 0;\n}",
      "C++": "#include <iostream>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    if (cin >> n) {\n        for (int i = n; i >= 1; i--) {\n            for (int j = 1; j <= i; j++) cout << j;\n            cout << \"\\n\";\n        }\n    }\n    return 0;\n}",
      "Java": "import java.util.Scanner;\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        if (sc.hasNextInt()) {\n            int n = sc.nextInt();\n            for (int i = n; i >= 1; i--) {\n                StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n                for (int j = 1; j <= i; j++) sb.append(j);\n                System.out.println(sb.toString());\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}",
      "Python3": "import sys\ndef main():\n    s = sys.stdin.read().strip()\n    if s:\n        n = int(s)\n        for i in range(n, 0, -1): print(''.join(str(j) for j in range(1, i + 1)))\nmain()",
      "JavaScript": "const fs = require('fs');\nfunction main() {\n    const s = fs.readFileSync(0, 'utf-8').trim();\n    if (s.length > 0) {\n        const n = parseInt(s, 10);\n        for (let i = n; i >= 1; i--) {\n            let line = '';\n            for (let j = 1; j <= i; j++) line += j;\n            console.log(line);\n        }\n    }\n}\nmain();"
    },
    "notes": "Ensure edge case and standard I/O format handling.",
    "editorial": "Print the required pattern line-by-line using nested loops based on line index and character offset."
